    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "893b463d_8a7b48e3",
        "filename": "microdroid/init.rc",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 101,
      "author": {
        "id": 1432579
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-19T21:30:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I wrote a simple test (aosp/2392904), and right now payload can\u0027t write to data. However, we will probably need to relax that to be able to run CTS tests inside Microdroid.\n\nWhether payload should have a scratch space to write some data to. I think it might be useful, but don\u0027t have strong use cases in mind.\n\nJiyong, WDYT?",
      "parentUuid": "2bb63573_d8c49300",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 101,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 101,
        "endChar": 68
      },
      "revId": "c890d4e4f18a01ea51c00fb47f7e691a3b75000a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "eb24b644_fe0b991d",
        "filename": "microdroid/init.rc",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 101,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-20T01:04:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good catch, Alan. We added this in the early days because some processes we brought from Android needed the existence of /data. I can\u0027t remember what were those, but this clearly isn\u0027t for the payload, which partially explains why the payload still can\u0027t write to here.\n\n\u003e we will probably need to relax\n\nDo we have to? The host-side test could execute the bionic tests as root.",
      "parentUuid": "893b463d_8a7b48e3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 101,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 101,
        "endChar": 68
      },
      "revId": "c890d4e4f18a01ea51c00fb47f7e691a3b75000a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ca703493_9e3e716c",
        "filename": "microdroid/init.rc",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 101,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-20T09:04:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s not doing any great harm I guess. But I\u0027d be ok with removing it.\nIf we want to use it for tests then we\u0027d need to think about how to organise that. Maybe you should ask for it in the config JSON.\nOn the whole I\u0027d rather not expose it to priv apps, absent some compelling use case.",
      "parentUuid": "eb24b644_fe0b991d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 101,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 101,
        "endChar": 68
      },
      "revId": "c890d4e4f18a01ea51c00fb47f7e691a3b75000a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "890d905c_f6a4b26d",
        "filename": "microdroid/init.rc",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 101,
      "author": {
        "id": 1432579
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-20T17:45:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Do we have to? The host-side test could execute the bionic tests as root.\n\nI\u0027d prefer to execute tests as close as possible to the environment as close to the environment they payload runs in.\n\nHaving said that, discussion about testing / using /data in payload is a bit tangental to this change. :)\n\nI think it\u0027s useful to enforce that we can\u0027t execute from writable partition, even if currently payload doesn\u0027t have access to it. WDYT?",
      "parentUuid": "ca703493_9e3e716c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 101,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 101,
        "endChar": 68
